AND VERY LITTLE SPACE.

217
00:09:05,975 --> 00:09:08,811
Robin: DOES ANYBODY WANT
TO SLEEP IN THE SLEEPING BAG?

218
00:09:08,811 --> 00:09:10,213
Elyse: NOT PARTICULARLY.

219
00:09:13,149 --> 00:09:18,154
Adrianne: FIVE PEOPLE
IN AN EXTREMELY SQUASHED ROOM,

220
00:09:18,154 --> 00:09:21,390
LIVING WITH A DIVA THAT TAKES
A VERY LONG TIME IN THERE.

221
00:09:21,390 --> 00:09:23,826
Shannon: WE ARE ALL LIVING
IN THIS SMALL ROOM TOGETHER.

222
00:09:23,826 --> 00:09:25,394
SOMETHING'S GONNA HAPPEN.

223
00:09:31,801 --> 00:09:35,004
♪♪♪

224
00:09:40,042 --> 00:09:42,111
Adrianne: I THINK EVERYBODY,
WHEN THEY SAW THE ROOM,

225
00:09:42,111 --> 00:09:43,145
WAS VERY DEPRESSED.

226
00:09:43,145 --> 00:09:44,080
Elyse: YOU GUYS
WANNA DRAW STRAWS

227
00:09:44,080 --> 00:09:45,781
FOR WHO'S ON THE FLOOR?

228
00:09:45,781 --> 00:09:49,452
Elyse: I IMMEDIATELY SAW
GIRLS EDGING TOWARD THE BEDS.

229
00:09:49,452 --> 00:09:52,021
SO I INSISTED THAT
WE DRAW NAMES.

230
00:09:52,021 --> 00:09:53,556
OKAY, SO THE FIRST THREE NAMES
WILL BE FOR THE THREE BEDS.

231
00:09:53,556 --> 00:09:56,192
Shannon: KESSE, YOU DRAW.

232
00:09:56,192 --> 00:09:58,094
- Robin: FOR THE FOUR BEDS.
- Kesse: NOT THE SLEEPING BAG.

233
00:09:58,094 --> 00:10:01,530
- Adrianne: THE AIR BED.
- Kesse: YEAH.

234
00:10:01,530 --> 00:10:03,065
MOI.

235
00:10:03,065 --> 00:10:05,034
Shannon: YEAH--
OH, IT WAS YOU.

236
00:10:05,034 --> 00:10:07,470
Adrianne: SHANNON. ELYSE.

237
00:10:07,470 --> 00:10:09,105
Kesse: ADRIANNE.

238
00:10:09,105 --> 00:10:10,539
Adrianne: HOLY CRAP.

239
00:10:10,539 --> 00:10:12,208
Elyse: I THOUGHT IT WAS
PRETTY FUNNY THAT ROBIN

240
00:10:12,208 --> 00:10:13,376
GOT THE AIR MATTRESS.

241
00:10:13,376 --> 00:10:16,812
Adrianne: ROBIN'S GOTTA
SLEEP ON THE FLOOR.

242
00:10:18,814 --> 00:10:21,083
Robin: MISS KESSE DID OFFER
TO SHARE HER BED WITH ME,

243
00:10:21,083 --> 00:10:24,420
BUT I MEAN, I'M NOT, YOU KNOW,
SO SPECIAL WHERE I CAN'T SLEEP

244
00:10:24,420 --> 00:10:25,554
ON THE AIR MATTRESS.

245
00:10:25,554 --> 00:10:29,292
♪♪♪

246
00:10:29,292 --> 00:10:31,127
Elyse: AFTER WE SETTLED
INTO OUR ROOM,

247
00:10:31,127 --> 00:10:33,129
WE JUST WANTED
TO HANG OUT AND TOOL AROUND

248
00:10:33,129 --> 00:10:34,830
AND CHECK OUT THE SIGHTS.

249
00:10:34,830 --> 00:10:36,332
Robin: YOU LOOK
AT THESE BUILDINGS

250
00:10:36,332 --> 00:10:37,967
AND YOU LOOK AT THESE FIXTURES,
AND YOU'RE LIKE, YOU KNOW,

251
00:10:37,967 --> 00:10:39,335
OH, MY GOODNESS.

252
00:10:39,335 --> 00:10:41,437
Adrianne: YOU GUYS,
I LOVE FRENCH CULTURE.

253
00:10:41,437 --> 00:10:43,039
Man: WHERE IS YOUR HUSBAND?

254
00:10:43,039 --> 00:10:45,107
Robin: I DON'T HAVE
A HUSBAND, UNFORTUNATELY.

255
00:10:45,107 --> 00:10:48,077
Man: OH, THAT'S OKAY.
YOU CAN STAY IN PARIS WITH ME.

256
00:10:48,077 --> 00:10:50,513
Shannon: THANKS.

257
00:10:51,380 --> 00:10:53,783
THAT GUY WAS ALL OVER MY FACE.

258
00:10:55,351 --> 00:10:57,420
Shannon: (shudders)

259
00:10:57,987 --> 00:11:01,524
♪♪♪

260
00:11:01,524 --> 00:11:03,826
Kesse: "TONIGHT I WILL
JOIN YOU FOR DINNER.

261
00:11:03,826 --> 00:11:06,829
BE READY IN THE LOBBY
AT 7 P.M. TYRA."

262
00:11:06,829 --> 00:11:08,097
Adrianne: I'VE BEEN WEARING
THE SAME UNDERWEAR

263
00:11:08,097 --> 00:11:10,399
FOR ALMOST 48 HOURS.

264
00:11:10,399 --> 00:11:13,035
IT'S JUST DISGUSTING.

265
00:11:14,770 --> 00:11:16,405
WHO'S GONNA CHANGE?

266
00:11:16,405 --> 00:11:18,507
THAT'S WHAT I'M WEARING.

267
00:11:18,507 --> 00:11:21,844
Shannon: A LITTLE, YOU KNOW,
NOT SHOWERED, A LITTLE, LIKE,

268
00:11:21,844 --> 00:11:24,246
YOU KNOW, SWEATY,
BUT WE JUST TRIED TO, LIKE,

269
00:11:24,246 --> 00:11:26,282
WASH OFF A LITTLE BIT,
GET A CHANGE OF CLOTHES.

270
00:11:26,282 --> 00:11:28,117
Adrianne: YOU GUYS,
I'VE NEVER FELT THIS ICKY

271
00:11:28,117 --> 00:11:29,819
IN MY ENTIRE LIFE.

272
00:11:29,819 --> 00:11:32,888
Robin: I AIN'T GOT
NO CLOTHES ON, MAN.

273
00:11:32,888 --> 00:11:34,523
Adrianne: ALL THE OTHER GIRLS
WERE VERY UNCOMFORTABLE

274
00:11:34,523 --> 00:11:36,559
WITH BEING NUDE
AROUND EACH OTHER.

275
00:11:36,559 --> 00:11:38,561
I MEAN, I JUST OUTRIGHT
TOLD THEM, I'M SORRY,

276
00:11:38,561 --> 00:11:40,229
WHEN I HAVE TO CHANGE,
I'M GOING TO.

277
00:11:40,229 --> 00:11:41,964
I DON'T CARE WHERE IT IS.

278
00:11:41,964 --> 00:11:44,533
YOU DON'T HAVE TO BE A LESBIAN
TO CHANGE IN FRONT

279
00:11:44,533 --> 00:11:46,869
OF YOUR FRIEND, YOU KNOW?

280
00:11:46,869 --> 00:11:50,906
- Elyse: (speaks French)
- Adrianne: HOW DO YOU SAY,

281
00:11:50,906 --> 00:11:53,209
"ADRIANNE HAS
ENORMOUS CHA-CHAS?"

282
00:11:53,209 --> 00:11:57,213
- Elyse: (speaks French)
- Adrianne: ELYSE, HOW BAD

283
00:11:57,213 --> 00:11:59,515
DOES YOUR COOCH SMELL,
HOW DO YOU SAY THAT?

284
00:11:59,515 --> 00:12:02,485
- Elyse: (speaks French)
- Robin: WHEN ADRIANNE SAYS

285
00:12:02,485 --> 00:12:05,521
THINGS THAT ARE INAPPROPRIATE,
I MIGHT LOOK AT HER IN A WAY

286
00:12:05,521 --> 00:12:08,424
THAT THE TEACHER WOULD LOOK
AT YOU IF YOU DID SOMETHING

287
00:12:08,424 --> 00:12:09,925
INAPPROPRIATE IN CLASS.

288
00:12:09,925 --> 00:12:11,027
I DON'T WANT TO HEAR THAT.

289
00:12:11,027 --> 00:12:12,995
I DON'T SPEAK LIKE THAT.

290
00:12:12,995 --> 00:12:15,297
I DON'T ACT LIKE THAT.

291
00:12:15,297 --> 00:12:17,500
Elyse: DO YOU GET IN TROUBLE
FOR THE THINGS YOU SAY?

292
00:12:17,500 --> 00:12:20,836
I TRY TO AVOID
DELIBERATELY PISSING OFF ROBIN,

293
00:12:20,836 --> 00:12:23,205
BUT ADRIANNE DEFINITELY DOES
DELIBERATELY DO IT,

294
00:12:23,205 --> 00:12:25,408
AND THAT'S GREAT
FOR ME TO WATCH.

295
00:12:25,408 --> 00:12:27,143
♪♪♪

296
00:12:30,846 --> 00:12:32,348
Tyra: BONJOUR. BONJOUR.

297
00:12:32,348 --> 00:12:33,916
All: BONJOUR.

298
00:12:33,916 --> 00:12:35,184
Tyra: HOW ARE YOU?

299
00:12:35,184 --> 00:12:37,386
Elyse: TYRA SHOWED UP
AT THE FRENCH RESTAURANT,

300
00:12:37,386 --> 00:12:41,290
AND SHE TOLD US A LITTLE BIT
ABOUT HER EXPERIENCE IN PARIS.

301
00:12:41,290 --> 00:12:45,995
Tyra: THIS CITY IS RESPONSIBLE
FOR THE SUCCESS OF MY CAREER.

302
00:12:45,995 --> 00:12:47,930
I WANTED TO PERSONALLY
INTRODUCE THE GIRLS TO THE CITY

303
00:12:47,930 --> 00:12:49,365
WHERE I STARTED MY CAREER.

304
00:12:49,365 --> 00:12:51,901
BUT IT TOOK A SCOUT FROM PARIS
BY THE NAME OF VERONIQUE

305
00:12:51,901 --> 00:12:54,170
WHO CAME TO LOS ANGELES
AND SAID, "I THINK YOU CAN BE

306
00:12:54,170 --> 00:12:55,771
A STAR, AND I WANT YOU TO COME
TO PARIS."

307
00:12:55,771 --> 00:12:56,939
AND THAT'S WHY IT WAS
SO IMPORTANT FOR ME

308
00:12:56,939 --> 00:12:58,240
TO HAVE YOU GUYS COME HERE.

309
00:12:58,240 --> 00:13:01,477
I INSISTED THAT THIS BE A PART
OF YOUR EXPERIENCE.

310
00:13:01,477 --> 00:13:04,146
AND IF YOU GUYS ARE MAD
AT YOUR APARTMENT,

311
00:13:04,146 --> 00:13:06,515
THAT WAS MY IDEA,
BECAUSE A MODEL'S APARTMENTS

312
00:13:06,515 --> 00:13:09,251
ARE CRAMPED AND TIGHT,
BUT I HAVE, LIKE,

313
00:13:09,251 --> 00:13:10,786
BITTERSWEET MEMORIES OF PARIS.

314
00:13:10,786 --> 00:13:12,555
BEING 17,
RIGHT OUT OF HIGH SCHOOL,

315
00:13:12,555 --> 00:13:15,057
GETTING ON A PLANE FOR
THE FIRST TIME BY MYSELF,

316
00:13:15,057 --> 00:13:16,959
AND I HUGGED MY MOM AND MY DAD,
AND THEY'RE LIKE,

317
00:13:16,959 --> 00:13:18,327
"ARE YOU OKAY?"

318
00:13:18,327 --> 00:13:20,196
AND I'M LIKE, "YEAH,"
AND THEN I TURNED AND I WAS...

319
00:13:20,196 --> 00:13:22,164
I JUST BOO-HOOED,
MY MOM DIDN'T KNOW THAT.

320
00:13:22,164 --> 00:13:24,100
THIS IS AN IMPORTANT MARKET.

321
00:13:24,100 --> 00:13:25,968
I WANT YOU GUYS,
WHOEVER THIS WINNER IS,

322
00:13:25,968 --> 00:13:27,970
TO WORK THE WORLD.

323
00:13:27,970 --> 00:13:29,905
Kesse: I JUST WANT TO BE OUT
ON MY OWN FOR AWHILE,

324
00:13:29,905 --> 00:13:33,342
AND EXPERIENCE, YOU KNOW,
THE REAL WORLD BY MYSELF.

325
00:13:33,342 --> 00:13:35,177
I MEAN, I WANT THIS REALLY BAD.

326
00:13:37,780 --> 00:13:41,117
"TOMORROW MORNING
WILL BE YOUR FIRST..." WHAT?

327
00:13:41,117 --> 00:13:43,018
"PARISIAN PHOTO SHOOT.

328
00:13:43,018 --> 00:13:45,521
BE READY AT 7:30 A.M.
IN THE LOBBY."

329
00:13:45,521 --> 00:13:48,424
Elyse: EVERYONE WAS
SO READY TO GO TO SLEEP.

330
00:13:50,960 --> 00:13:53,462
Adrianne: I CAN'T MOVE.
EXHAUSTION.

331
00:13:53,462 --> 00:13:56,132
Robin: RIGHT,
LET MAMA WASH HER FACE.

332
00:13:56,132 --> 00:13:57,867
Adrianne: ROBIN HAS TO
SLEEP ON THE FLOOR--

333
00:13:57,867 --> 00:14:00,369
MISS PAGEANTRY.

334
00:14:03,105 --> 00:14:07,309
(blow dryer running)

335
00:14:07,309 --> 00:14:08,944
Adrianne: I THINK
SHE TOOK IT OUT ON US,

336
00:14:08,944 --> 00:14:12,014
BECAUSE SHE WAS UP VERY LATE

337
00:14:12,014 --> 00:14:14,250
BLOW DRYING HER HAIR,
SMASHING ABOUT.

338
00:14:14,250 --> 00:14:15,885
Robin: EVERY GIRL
WASHED THEIR HAIR,

339
00:14:15,885 --> 00:14:18,487
AND I HAD TO BLOW DRY MINE.

340
00:14:18,487 --> 00:14:22,124
(blow dryer running)

341
00:14:22,124 --> 00:14:23,859
Elyse: I THINK
THAT ROBIN HERSELF

342
00:14:23,859 --> 00:14:26,295
DOESN'T HAVE A VERY GOOD IDEA
OF WHAT A CHRISTIAN IS.

343
00:14:26,295 --> 00:14:29,932
(blow dryer running)

344
00:14:29,932 --> 00:14:32,334
♪♪♪

345
00:14:32,334 --> 00:14:34,403
Shannon: TODAY, UM,
A PHOTO SHOOT IN PARIS.

346
00:14:34,403 --> 00:14:37,139
IT WAS OUR FIRST
PARISIAN PHOTO SHOOT.

347
00:14:40,009 --> 00:14:42,945
Kesse: OH, MY GOSH,
THERE'S NOTHING LIKE IT.

348
00:14:43,479 --> 00:14:46,048
Adrianne: THIS IS
INSANELY BEAUTIFUL.

349
00:14:46,048 --> 00:14:47,283
Kesse: EIFFEL TOWER.

350
00:14:47,283 --> 00:14:48,984
OH, IT'S SO BEAUTIFUL.

351
00:14:48,984 --> 00:14:51,353
LOOKIN' AT IT,
IT IS JUST LIKE, "WOW."

352
00:14:51,353 --> 00:14:53,055
Iderlin: SO
LET'S TRY THIS ONE ON NOW

353
00:14:53,055 --> 00:14:55,090
AND SEE IF THIS ONE WORKS.

354
00:14:55,090 --> 00:14:58,794
Kesse: OUR FITTING WAS BRAS--
BRAS AND UNDERWEAR--SO IT WAS

355
00:14:58,794 --> 00:15:00,496
A PHOTO SHOOT FOR WONDERBRA.

356
00:15:00,496 --> 00:15:02,431
Robin: THE PHOTO SHOOTS
ARE GETTING MORE

357
00:15:02,431 --> 00:15:04,800
AND MORE INTERESTING,
FOR LACK OF BETTER WORDS.

358
00:15:04,800 --> 00:15:06,202
Elyse: CAN WE SEE YOUR BRA?

359
00:15:06,202 --> 00:15:08,938
Shannon: YOU CAN SEE MY BRA,
BUT ANYTHING ELSE, YOU AIN'T...

360
00:15:08,938 --> 00:15:11,040
Adrianne: AH, HA HA HA.

361
00:15:11,040 --> 00:15:13,943
I HAVE NO IDEA WHAT IT IS
THAT SHANNON'S HOLDING INSIDE.

362
00:15:13,943 --> 00:15:16,545
I THINK SHE'S JUST SO CRAZY
BECAUSE SHE'S NEVER

363
00:15:16,545 --> 00:15:19,248
DONE ANYTHING--
SHE'S NEVER TOUCHED HERSELF.

364
00:15:19,248 --> 00:15:21,217
SHE'S NEVER WATCHED A PORN.

365
00:15:21,217 --> 00:15:23,018
SHE'S NEVER DONE ANYTHING.

366
00:15:23,018 --> 00:15:24,520
Shannon: I THINK
THAT MY UNCOVERED BODY

367
00:15:24,520 --> 00:15:27,423
IS FOR ONE PERSON ONLY,
THAT'S MY HUSBAND.

368
00:15:27,423 --> 00:15:28,857
SO I DON'T KNOW.

369
00:15:28,857 --> 00:15:30,559
I JUST DON'T THINK
IT'S FOR THE WORLD TO SEE.

370
00:15:30,559 --> 00:15:33,862
NO ONE IN THE HOUSE IS--
EVERYONE IN THE HOUSE--

371
00:15:33,862 --> 00:15:35,431
WELL, I MEAN, EVERYONE'S NOT
AS COMFORTABLE WALKING AROUND

372
00:15:35,431 --> 00:15:36,532
IN THONG UNDERWEAR
LIKE YOU ARE.

373
00:15:36,532 --> 00:15:38,100
Adrianne: HOW ARE YOU GUYS
GONNA BE MODELS?

374
00:15:38,100 --> 00:15:40,436
Jay: HELLO. DO YOU THINK
IT'S OKAY TO MASTURBATE?

375
00:15:40,436 --> 00:15:41,470
WE ALREADY
HAD THIS CONVERSATION,

376
00:15:41,470 --> 00:15:43,072
BUT I WANNA SEE
WHAT YOUR OPINION IS.

377
00:15:43,072 --> 00:15:46,108
Shannon: I'VE NEVER DONE IT
BEFORE, BUT I DON'T KNOW.

378
00:15:46,108 --> 00:15:48,177
I KNEW A GUY, WHAT HE DID,
BUT I--

379
00:15:48,177 --> 00:15:49,945
Jay: YEAH, BUT WE'RE NOT
TALKING ABOUT MEN RIGHT NOW.

380
00:15:49,945 --> 00:15:52,014
Shannon: I DIDN'T KNOW WE
COULD DO IT, LIKE, TO OURSELVES.

381
00:15:54,917 --> 00:15:56,285
Robin: HI.

382
00:15:56,285 --> 00:15:58,020
Michel: HI, GIRLS.

383
00:15:58,020 --> 00:16:00,222
MY NAME IS MICHEL HADDI,
NICE TO MEET YOU LADIES.

384
00:16:00,222 --> 00:16:01,490
Elyse: NICE TO MEET YOU, TOO.

385
00:16:01,490 --> 00:16:03,859
Michel: I HOPE THAT TODAY
YOU'RE READY TO RUMBLE.

386
00:16:03,859 --> 00:16:07,062
I HOPE, BE GOOD, BE BAD,
BE AS BAD AS YOU CAN BE.

387
00:16:07,062 --> 00:16:08,998
ALL RIGHT?

388
00:16:08,998 --> 00:16:10,466
Elyse: WE ALL GOT IN
BRAS AND UNDERWEAR

389
00:16:10,466 --> 00:16:12,301
AND GOT OUR MAKEUP
AND HAIR DONE.

390
00:16:12,301 --> 00:16:14,136
AND THEN THE SURPRISE
WAS THAT THERE WOULD BE

391
00:16:14,136 --> 00:16:15,971
A MALE MODEL POSING WITH US.

392
00:16:15,971 --> 00:16:18,807
Shannon: OH, MY WORD!

393
00:16:18,807 --> 00:16:22,845
I WALKED IN THE FIRST ROOM,
I TURN AROUND, AND I SEE THIS

394
00:16:22,845 --> 00:16:24,413
REALLY MUSCULAR GUY IN BOXERS.

395
00:16:24,413 --> 00:16:25,814
Man: HOW YOU DOING?

396
00:16:25,814 --> 00:16:27,816
- Shannon: GOOD.
- Man: I'M BRAD.

397
00:16:27,816 --> 00:16:29,051
- Shannon: SHANNON.
- Brad: NICE TO MEET YOU.

398
00:16:29,051 --> 00:16:32,488
Shannon: OH, MY WORD!
YOU GUYS, NO!

399
00:16:32,488 --> 00:16:34,890
IT WAS BRAD PINKERT,
THE GUY I'VE BEEN TALKING ABOUT

400
00:16:34,890 --> 00:16:36,258
THIS WHOLE TRIP.

401
00:16:36,258 --> 00:16:37,459
I HAD A POSTER OF HIM
IN MY ROOM.

402
00:16:37,459 --> 00:16:39,328
ARE YOU, LIKE, THE MODEL?

403
00:16:39,328 --> 00:16:41,196
Brad: I BELIEVE SO, YES.

404
00:16:41,196 --> 00:16:44,466
Shannon: YOU GUYS GOTTA BE...

405
00:16:44,466 --> 00:16:46,468
OH, MY GOSH,
I DON'T KNOW WHETHER TO SMILE,

406
00:16:46,468 --> 00:16:49,004
WHETHER TO GET RED, WHETHER TO,
LIKE, TURN AROUND AND LEAVE.

407
00:16:49,004 --> 00:16:50,239
Michel: OKAY,
LET'S WORK, GUYS.

408
00:16:50,239 --> 00:16:51,473
LET'S DO SOME PHOTOGRAPH.

409
00:16:51,473 --> 00:16:53,475
THAT'S IT.

410
00:16:53,475 --> 00:16:55,110
ENJOY IT.

411
00:16:55,110 --> 00:16:56,378
Shannon: I WAS GRABBING HIM
OR SOMETHING, LIKE,

412
00:16:56,378 --> 00:16:57,212
HE HAD TO PUT
HIS ARMS AROUND ME,

413
00:16:57,212 --> 00:16:58,514
AND I WAS LIKE,
"I'VE NEVER BEEN

414
00:16:58,514 --> 00:17:00,282
IN THIS POSITION BEFORE."

415
00:17:00,282 --> 00:17:02,484
Michel: OKAY, BITE HIM.
BITE--GO FOR IT.

416
00:17:02,484 --> 00:17:03,352
VERY GOOD, LET'S SEE IT.

417
00:17:05,119 --> 00:17:07,923
AND YOU CAN BE CLOSER.

418
00:17:07,923 --> 00:17:09,558
NOTHING IS GOING TO HAPPEN
TO YOU, I PROMISE.

419
00:17:09,558 --> 00:17:11,193
Shannon: AND HE'S GOT
SOME MUSCLES, MAN!

420
00:17:11,193 --> 00:17:13,829
HE'S GOT SOME MUSCLES.

421
00:17:13,962 --> 00:17:15,897
Michel: THAT'S VERY GOOD.

422
00:17:15,897 --> 00:17:17,499
Shannon: (giggles)

423
00:17:18,200 --> 00:17:19,501
OH, THIS IS LOVELY.

424
00:17:19,501 --> 00:17:21,470
Michel: NO, NO, IT'S ALL RIGHT.
THAT'S IT.

425
00:17:21,470 --> 00:17:26,909
SHANNON IS JUST A BIT LOST,

426
00:17:26,909 --> 00:17:29,278
BUT SHE'S GOT
A VERY BEAUTIFUL FACE.

427
00:17:29,278 --> 00:17:33,782
Brad: I HOPE I WAS
EVERYTHING SHE THOUGHT

428
00:17:33,782 --> 00:17:35,017
I WAS GOING TO BE.

429
00:17:35,017 --> 00:17:36,185
Shannon: I'LL SEE YOU LATER.

430
00:17:36,185 --> 00:17:37,820
Brad: ALL RIGHT, DEFINITELY.
HAVE FUN.

431
00:17:37,820 --> 00:17:40,055
Michel: HEAD TO HEAD,
STRAIGHT ON.

432
00:17:40,055 --> 00:17:43,092
I WANT TWO FACES
CLOSE TO EACH OTHER, RIGHT?

433
00:17:43,092 --> 00:17:44,226
VERY GOOD,
STAY LIKE YOU ARE.

434
00:17:44,226 --> 00:17:45,094
THAT'S VERY GOOD,
DON'T MOVE.

435
00:17:45,094 --> 00:17:47,496
STAY LIKE YOU ARE.

436
00:17:47,496 --> 00:17:49,331
VERY GOOD.

437
00:17:49,331 --> 00:17:52,801
THAT'S GOOD.

438
00:17:52,801 --> 00:17:54,303
Elyse: POSING WITH BRAD
WAS LIKE POSING WITH A STATUE.

439
00:17:54,303 --> 00:17:55,804
I WASN'T UNCOMFORTABLE AT ALL.

440
00:17:57,539 --> 00:17:59,007
Michel: SHE'S FABULOUS.

441
00:17:59,007 --> 00:18:00,342
YEAH, ELYSE IS LIKE...

442
00:18:00,342 --> 00:18:02,111
SHE'S LIKE A LITTLE FAWN,
YOU KNOW, COMING OUT

443
00:18:02,111 --> 00:18:04,279
OF A WALT DISNEY MOVIE.

444
00:18:04,279 --> 00:18:06,882
YOU HAVE TO TALK THE TALK
AND WALK THE WALK.

445
00:18:06,882 --> 00:18:10,085
YOUR LEGS HAS TO BE STRONG.

446
00:18:10,085 --> 00:18:13,555
GO SHOW ME,
SHOW ME LONG LEGS, LONG.

447
00:18:13,555 --> 00:18:14,556
Kesse: YOU KNOW, I WAS TRYING
TO DO MY BEST TO,

448
00:18:14,556 --> 00:18:16,458
YOU KNOW, WHATEVER,
BUT I DIDN'T THINK I WAS

449
00:18:16,458 --> 00:18:18,260
DOING IT HOW HE WANTED IT.

450
00:18:18,260 --> 00:18:19,828
Michel: YOUR HAIR THERE.

451
00:18:19,828 --> 00:18:20,863
VERY GOOD.

452
00:18:20,863 --> 00:18:23,365
YOU HAVE TO MOVE, OKAY? NOW.

453
00:18:28,504 --> 00:18:30,472
Michel: HOME FREE, THAT'S IT.

454
00:18:30,472 --> 00:18:33,976
SHE'S TOO SCARED
THAT'S THE PROBLEM,

455
00:18:33,976 --> 00:18:35,277
AND SHE'S NOT CONFIDENT.

456
00:18:35,277 --> 00:18:37,946
Adrianne: DON'T YOU LOVE
DOING THAT?

457
00:18:37,946 --> 00:18:39,448
MY BOOBS.

458
00:18:39,448 --> 00:18:40,783
Iderlin: THANK YOU.

459
00:18:40,783 --> 00:18:41,817
Michel: STAY LIKE YOU ARE.

460
00:18:41,817 --> 00:18:43,952
VERY GOOD.

461
00:18:43,952 --> 00:18:47,156
Adrianne: WE'RE SUPPOSED TO
BE ON FIRE, AND I WAS.

462
00:18:47,156 --> 00:18:50,426
Michel: VERY GOOD,
STAY LIKE YOU ARE.

463
00:18:50,426 --> 00:18:53,862
SHE'S GOT IT,
AS SIMPLE AS THAT.

464
00:18:53,862 --> 00:18:55,964
- Brad: HI, NICE TO MEET YOU.
- Robin: NICE TO MEET YOU, TOO.

465
00:18:55,964 --> 00:18:59,001
Michel: WRAP YOUR HANDS
AROUND HER.

466
00:18:59,001 --> 00:19:01,003
TURN YOUR BODY A BIT MORE,
A BIT MORE, A BIT MORE.

467
00:19:01,003 --> 00:19:04,006
Robin: I DIDN'T KNOW
WHAT THE SETUP WAS WITH THE GUY.

468
00:19:04,006 --> 00:19:06,241
I WAS A LITTLE, YOU KNOW,
UNCOMFORTABLE AT FIRST

469
00:19:06,241 --> 00:19:10,078
NOT KNOWING THE SETTING
OF THE SCENE OR WHATEVER.

470
00:19:10,078 --> 00:19:11,447
Michel: JUST RELAX.

471
00:19:11,447 --> 00:19:13,549
Robin: YOU KNOW, ONCE I,
LIKE I SAID, SAID MY PRAYER

472
00:19:13,549 --> 00:19:17,319
AND CLEARED MY MIND, YOU KNOW,
SOME THINGS YOU DON'T LIKE,

473
00:19:17,319 --> 00:19:19,388
BUT YOU DO BECAUSE OF THE JOB.

474
00:19:19,388 --> 00:19:20,255
Michel: ROBIN IS
A FABULOUS GIRL,

475
00:19:20,255 --> 00:19:21,290
BUT YOU KNOW WHAT?

476
00:19:21,290 --> 00:19:23,125
SHE DOESN'T TRUST HER OWN BODY.

477
00:19:27,429 --> 00:19:30,399
Adrianne: WERE YOU
UNCOMFORTABLE, THOUGH, SHANNON?

478
00:19:30,399 --> 00:19:33,402
NO, BECAUSE YOU'VE BEEN DREAMING
OVER THAT GUY FOR SO LONG.

479
00:19:33,402 --> 00:19:34,436
Shannon: NO.

480
00:19:34,436 --> 00:19:36,438
Adrianne: YES, YOU HAVE.

481
00:19:36,438 --> 00:19:37,906
Shannon: I WAS A LITTLE BIT
NERVOUS, BECAUSE I'VE NEVER

482
00:19:37,906 --> 00:19:39,775
HAD A PHOTO SHOOT WITH A GUY,
ESPECIALLY ONE THAT

483
00:19:39,775 --> 00:19:41,176
I'VE BEEN WANTING TO MEET.

484
00:19:41,176 --> 00:19:42,478
AND THE FIRST TIME WE MEET
EACH OTHER, WE'RE, LIKE,

485
00:19:42,478 --> 00:19:44,012
IN OUR, LIKE, UNDERWEAR.

486
00:19:44,012 --> 00:19:45,247
Adrianne: (speaking French)

487
00:19:45,247 --> 00:19:47,316
- Shannon: (speaking French)
- (knock on door)

488
00:19:47,316 --> 00:19:49,952
Adrianne: HELLO.

489
00:19:49,952 --> 00:19:51,487
Shannon: OH!

490
00:19:51,487 --> 00:19:53,088
- Kesse: HEY, BRAD.
- Brad: HOW'S EVERYBODY FEEL?

491
00:19:53,088 --> 00:19:54,456
HOW'D IT GO?

492
00:19:54,456 --> 00:19:56,058
- Adrianne: ALL RIGHT.
- Shannon: GOOD.

493
00:19:56,058 --> 00:19:57,292
Brad: IT WENT OKAY
WITH ME, TOO.

494
00:19:57,292 --> 00:19:58,827
YOU GUYS WANNA GO OUT
TO DINNER LATER?

495
00:19:58,827 --> 00:20:01,497
Shannon: YEAH!
WE'RE ALWAYS HUNGRY.

496
00:20:01,497 --> 00:20:05,434
Brad: I'M NOT REALLY SURE,
BUT I KNOW WE'LL HAVE SOME FUN.

497
00:20:05,434 --> 00:20:07,302
ALL RIGHT,
I'LL SEE YOU GUYS.

498
00:20:07,302 --> 00:20:08,136
- Kesse: THANKS, BRAD.
- Adrianne: BYE.

499
00:20:08,136 --> 00:20:09,538
- Elyse: BYE, BRAD.

500
00:20:09,872 --> 00:20:12,107
Shannon: (squeals)
I'VE BEEN ON A FEW DATES

501
00:20:12,107 --> 00:20:14,276
BUT NOT LIKE "DATE" DATES.

502
00:20:14,276 --> 00:20:15,310
YEAH, I GET NERVOUS.

503
00:20:15,310 --> 00:20:17,045
WE'RE GOIN' OUT TO DINNER.

504
00:20:17,045 --> 00:20:18,514
WE'RE GOIN' OUT TO DINNER.

505
00:20:18,514 --> 00:20:19,548
WHOO!

506
00:20:19,548 --> 00:20:23,485
Elyse: IT'S GONNA BE SO FUN.

507
00:20:23,485 --> 00:20:26,154
Shannon: I DON'T HAVE
ANY CLOTHES. NO!

508
00:20:29,191 --> 00:20:31,623
♪♪♪

509
00:20:31,623 --> 00:20:33,092
Elyse: WHEN WE GOT BACK
TO THE APARTMENT,

510
00:20:33,092 --> 00:20:34,793
WE HAD TO CHANGE OUR CLOTHES
REALLY QUICKLY.

511
00:20:34,793 --> 00:20:36,295
AND WE WENT TO DINNER WITH BRAD.

512
00:20:36,295 --> 00:20:39,098
Robin: I'LL BET
YOU'RE NERVOUS.

513
00:20:39,098 --> 00:20:41,900
Brad: NO, I'M FINE.

514
00:20:41,900 --> 00:20:43,802
Robin: SO WHAT DID THEY
TELL YOU ABOUT MISS SHANNON?

515
00:20:43,802 --> 00:20:45,971
Brad: THEY JUST SAID,
"SOMEBODY HAS A CRUSH ON YOU"

516
00:20:45,971 --> 00:20:50,008
OR "SOMEBODY HAS YOUR PICTURE
AND KNOWS OF YOU."

517
00:20:50,008 --> 00:20:52,077
AND I WAS FLATTERED.

518
00:20:52,077 --> 00:20:53,612
Robin: SO WHAT DO YOU THINK
OF MISS SHANNON?

519
00:20:53,612 --> 00:20:56,014
Shannon: I'M SITTING
RIGHT HERE.

520
00:20:56,014 --> 00:20:57,349
Brad: I TOLD 'EM
I WAS STUNNED.

521
00:20:57,349 --> 00:20:58,884
Robin: WELL, I WAS JUST
TRYING TO GET MISS SHANNON

522
00:20:58,884 --> 00:21:01,120
TO TALK MORE, BUT YOU KNOW,
SHE DOESN'T' REALLY TALK

523
00:21:01,120 --> 00:21:02,321
A WHOLE LOT AROUND GUYS.

524
00:21:02,321 --> 00:21:03,389
Brad: DID WE HAVE FUN TODAY?

525
00:21:03,389 --> 00:21:04,623
Elyse: DID YOU?

526
00:21:04,623 --> 00:21:05,657
Brad: OH, I HAD FUN.

527
00:21:05,657 --> 00:21:07,059
YOU KNOW, IT WAS TIRING.

528
00:21:07,059 --> 00:21:10,729
BUT A MAN'S GOTTA DO
WHAT A MAN'S GOTTA DO, I GUESS.

529
00:21:10,996 --> 00:21:12,331
Robin: WHAT'S
YOUR FAVORITE BOOK?

530
00:21:12,331 --> 00:21:15,667
Brad: FAVORITE BOOK?

531
00:21:15,667 --> 00:21:16,969
ONE OF THEM'S THE BIBLE.

532
00:21:16,969 --> 00:21:18,137
Adrianne: WHAT'S ANOTHER ONE?

533
00:21:18,137 --> 00:21:20,639
Brad: ANOTHER BOOK?

534
00:21:20,639 --> 00:21:21,907
Shannon: THERE'S
NO CHICKEN ON HERE.

535
00:21:21,907 --> 00:21:24,777
Brad: I DON'T READ TOO MUCH.

536
00:21:24,777 --> 00:21:26,078
Adrianne: I TOLD SHANNON--
SHE THOUGHT,

537
00:21:26,078 --> 00:21:28,013
"OH, THIS GUY LIKES THE BIBLE.

538
00:21:28,013 --> 00:21:30,215
HE'S GONNA BE SO NICE."

539
00:21:30,215 --> 00:21:33,685
WELL, IN HIS LITTLE, LIKE,
SPREAD SHEET IN "COSMO GIRL!,"

540
00:21:33,685 --> 00:21:35,854
IT SAID THAT HIS FAVORITE MOVIE
WAS "BOOGIE NIGHTS."

541
00:21:35,854 --> 00:21:37,923
Robin: YOU JUST, YOU KNOW,
GO OUT AND HAVE FUN, WHATEVER.

542
00:21:37,923 --> 00:21:39,224
JUST GO.

543
00:21:39,224 --> 00:21:40,392
Shannon: OKAY, NO.

544
00:21:40,392 --> 00:21:41,994
I DON'T WANNA GO BY MYSELF.

545
00:21:41,994 --> 00:21:44,329
Adrianne: WELL,
BRAD'S GONNA BE THERE.

546
00:21:44,329 --> 00:21:46,064
Robin: GIRL, COME ON.

547
00:21:46,064 --> 00:21:48,167
YEAH, BRAD WILL SHOW YOU
THE CITY FOR A LITTLE WHILE.

548
00:21:48,167 --> 00:21:49,868
Elyse: I THINK
SHANNON SUBMITTED TO PRESSURES

549
00:21:49,868 --> 00:21:51,203
FROM ROBIN.

550
00:21:51,203 --> 00:21:53,772
ROBIN SAID
THAT IT WOULDN'T COMPLY

551
00:21:53,772 --> 00:21:55,674
WITH ETIQUETTE IF SHANNON
DIDN'T GO OUT ON A DATE

552
00:21:55,674 --> 00:21:57,176
WITH BRAD AFTER DINNER.

553
00:21:57,176 --> 00:22:00,179
Robin: SHE HAD HIS PICTURE
ON HER CANOPY.

554
00:22:00,179 --> 00:22:02,147
THAT'S LIKE A NICE LITTLE WAY
OF SAYING THANK YOU.

555
00:22:02,147 --> 00:22:05,184
Woman: (singing in French)

556
00:22:11,723 --> 00:22:13,225
Shannon: AT TIMES,
I ENJOY BEING SINGLE,

557
00:22:13,225 --> 00:22:15,093
'CAUSE I'VE BEEN SINGLE
FOR I DON'T KNOW HOW LONG.

558
00:22:15,093 --> 00:22:17,296
BUT DEEP DOWN I THINK THAT I
WOULD ENJOY HAVING A BOYFRIEND

559
00:22:17,296 --> 00:22:19,064
JUST BECAUSE I'M A ROMANTIC.

560
00:22:19,064 --> 00:22:20,799
Woman: (singing in French)

561
00:22:33,178 --> 00:22:34,246
Shannon: I'M SO EMBARRASSED.

562
00:22:34,246 --> 00:22:35,280
Elyse: WHY?

563
00:22:35,280 --> 00:22:37,749
Kesse: WHAT HAPPENED?

564
00:22:37,749 --> 00:22:39,384
Shannon: WELL, I'M GONNA TELL
Y'ALL THE ENDING.

565
00:22:39,384 --> 00:22:41,954
I WAS LEAVING,
AND YOU KNOW HOW

566
00:22:41,954 --> 00:22:44,723
SOMETIMES YOU KISS ONCE,
SOMETIMES WOMEN GIVE TWO?

567
00:22:44,723 --> 00:22:47,125
WELL, I GAVE HIM ONE
AND HE WAS LIKE,

568
00:22:47,125 --> 00:22:50,162
"NOW YOU GOTTA GIVE TWO."

569
00:22:50,162 --> 00:22:53,165
Robin: SO WE GOTTA
DRESS TO IMPRESS TOMORROW

570
00:22:53,165 --> 00:22:55,267
WITH YOUR PORTFOLIO.

571
00:22:55,267 --> 00:22:57,736
Shannon: "BE READY
TOMORROW MORNING AT 9:00 A.M.--

572
00:22:57,736 --> 00:22:59,171
9 IN THE MORNING.

573
00:22:59,171 --> 00:23:02,808
BE DRESSED TO IMPRESS
ALONG WITH YOUR PORTFOLIO.

574
00:23:02,808 --> 00:23:04,643
MAKE THE MOST OF THE DAY,
BECAUSE TOMORROW NIGHT,

575
00:23:04,643 --> 00:23:06,345
ONE OF YOU
WILL HAVE TO GO HOME."

576
00:23:06,345 --> 00:23:09,748
Kesse: I LOVE THEM
LIKE WE'VE BEEN FRIENDS FOREVER.

577
00:23:09,748 --> 00:23:11,316
AND IT'S GETTING HARDER,
YOU KNOW,

578
00:23:11,316 --> 00:23:13,285
KNOWING THAT SOMEBODY'S LEAVING.

579
00:23:13,285 --> 00:23:15,053
Adrianne: WELL,
ALL I'VE GOT TO SAY IS

580
00:23:15,053 --> 00:23:17,956
IF I'M GONNA BE ELIMINATED,

581
00:23:17,956 --> 00:23:20,158
I'D RATHER BE ELIMINATED
IN PARIS.

582
00:23:27,766 --> 00:23:29,301
Robin: TODAY
WE'RE GOING TO DO GO SEES.

583
00:23:29,301 --> 00:23:31,870
AND YOU GO SEE A CLIENT,

584
00:23:31,870 --> 00:23:36,275
AND THEY GIVE YOU FEEDBACK
ON WHETHER OR NOT THEY LIKE YOU.

585
00:23:36,275 --> 00:23:38,310
Shannon: I AM READY
AND EXCITED.

586
00:23:38,310 --> 00:23:41,046
EVEN THOUGH IT COULD BE
A PRETTY NERVE-RACKING DAY.

587
00:23:45,918 --> 00:23:47,886
- Woman: HELLO.
- All: HI.

588
00:23:47,886 --> 00:23:49,988
- Woman: HOW ARE YOU?
- Shannon: GOOD.

589
00:23:49,988 --> 00:23:53,825
Marilyn: MY NAME'S MARILYN,
AND I'M THE HEAD OF THE AGENCY.

590
00:23:53,825 --> 00:23:56,128
TO YOU, IT'S VERY IMPORTANT
TO START IN PARIS.

591
00:23:56,128 --> 00:23:58,363
ALL TOP MODELS
HAVE STARTED HERE.

592
00:23:58,363 --> 00:24:00,866
AS PART OF THE TEST,
WE'RE GOING TO DO GO SEES TODAY.

593
00:24:00,866 --> 00:24:02,668
OKAY, NOW LET'S GO
AND SEE EMMA--

594
00:24:02,668 --> 00:24:04,836
SHE'S IN THE OTHER ROOM--
AND GO IN TO MEET HER.

595
00:24:04,836 --> 00:24:06,104
Emma: HELLO, I'M EMMA.

596
00:24:06,104 --> 00:24:09,975
I LOOK AFTER THE NEW FACES
DIVISION AT MARILYN'S.

597
00:24:09,975 --> 00:24:12,144
YOU'VE GOT FIVE GO AND SEES
THAT YOU'RE GONNA DO

598
00:24:12,144 --> 00:24:15,948
THIS AFTERNOON
BETWEEN 2:00 AND 7:00.

599
00:24:15,948 --> 00:24:18,116
EACH ONE'S GOT A DIFFERENT TIME.

600
00:24:18,116 --> 00:24:20,218
SO ONE'S GONNA BE BETWEEN
2:00 AND 3:00,

601
00:24:20,218 --> 00:24:21,987
ONE'S BETWEEN 3:00 AND 4:00.

602
00:24:21,987 --> 00:24:26,158
YOU HAVE TO GET TO ALL OF THEM,
AND YOU ALSO HAVE TO GO ALONE.

603
00:24:26,158 --> 00:24:28,260
NOW I'M GONNA EXPLAIN TO YOU
HOW YOU'RE GONNA

604
00:24:28,260 --> 00:24:30,596
GET AROUND PARIS
AND HOW YOU'RE GONNA GET BY

605
00:24:30,596 --> 00:24:31,730
ON THE MéTRO.

606
00:24:31,730 --> 00:24:34,032
WITHIN PARIS
ARE DIFFERENT AREAS,

607
00:24:34,032 --> 00:24:36,068
WHICH ARE CALLED
ARRONDISSEMENTS.

608
00:24:36,068 --> 00:24:38,136
EACH TIME, YOU'RE GONNA HAVE
A CHOICE WHETHER TO GO

609
00:24:38,136 --> 00:24:40,238
NORTH OR SOUTH, EAST OR WEST.

610
00:24:40,238 --> 00:24:42,274
NOW THERE MIGHT BE
RUE PARMENTIE,

611
00:24:42,274 --> 00:24:46,612
THERE MIGHT BE AVENUE PARMENTIE,
THERE MIGHT BE PLACE PARMENTIE.

612
00:24:46,612 --> 00:24:50,816
HAVE YOU GOT THE GRID KEY?
IT'S LIKE "G-4" OR "F-14."

613
00:24:50,816 --> 00:24:54,052
SO IN YOUR MAPS,
YOU GO TO 18.

614
00:24:54,052 --> 00:24:55,654
BLUE LINE'S NUMBER 2 LINE.

615
00:24:55,654 --> 00:24:57,689
CONCONTE IS ON
THE NUMBER 1 LINE.

616
00:24:57,689 --> 00:24:58,924
IT'S RIGHT IN THE MIDDLE.

617
00:24:58,924 --> 00:25:00,225
IT'S WHEN YOU GET IN
THE MéTRO STATION,

618
00:25:00,225 --> 00:25:02,160
YOU FOLLOW THAT DIRECTION.

619
00:25:02,160 --> 00:25:04,730
OKAY, DO YOU HAVE ANY QUESTIONS?

620
00:25:04,730 --> 00:25:08,867
(no audio)

621
00:25:08,867 --> 00:25:10,369
Shannon: THAT IS JUST
SO MIND-BOGGLING

622
00:25:10,369 --> 00:25:12,771
FOR ME TO COMPREHEND.

623
00:25:12,771 --> 00:25:14,206
Emma: YOU'VE GOT FOUR HOURS
TO DO THIS,

624
00:25:14,206 --> 00:25:16,174
AND YOU'VE GOT FIVE CASTINGS.

625
00:25:16,174 --> 00:25:17,209
REMEMBER, THESE ARE CLIENTS.

626
00:25:17,209 --> 00:25:18,610
THEY'RE WAITING TO SEE YOU.

627
00:25:18,610 --> 00:25:20,178
YOU'VE GOT TO GET TO SEE THEM.

628
00:25:20,178 --> 00:25:21,380
Robin: I DIDN'T WANT
TO TAKE THE MéTRO

629
00:25:21,380 --> 00:25:22,981
AND COULDN'T SEE
WHY WE JUST COULDN'T TAKE A CAB.

630
00:25:22,981 --> 00:25:25,083
I MEAN, YOU KNOW, THAT'S, LIKE,
MY WAY OF LOOKING AT THINGS.

631
00:25:25,083 --> 00:25:28,987
Emma: THE MéTRO IS A BIG "M"
OR MéTROPOLITAN.

632
00:25:28,987 --> 00:25:31,189
GET INTO THE MéTRO
AND THEN GET GOING.

633
00:25:31,189 --> 00:25:33,358
SPLIT UP AND JUST GET GOING.

634
00:25:33,358 --> 00:25:35,293
♪♪♪

635
00:25:40,699 --> 00:25:43,735
Adrianne: OKAY. SO...

636
00:25:43,735 --> 00:25:45,237
THIS IS GOING TO BE A BITCH.

637
00:25:50,942 --> 00:25:52,711
Kesse: I WAS CONFUSED,
I DIDN'T KNOW WHAT I WAS DOING.

638
00:25:52,711 --> 00:25:53,645
I WAS JUST TRYING TO HURRY UP.

639
00:25:55,814 --> 00:25:57,849
(laughs)

640
00:25:57,849 --> 00:25:58,984
♪♪♪

641
00:26:05,190 --> 00:26:06,992
Elyse: I'M REALLY A BEGINNER.

642
00:26:06,992 --> 00:26:08,260
Man: COOL.

643
00:26:08,260 --> 00:26:09,594
Elyse: BUT I'VE BEEN TRYING
TO LEARN.

644
00:26:09,594 --> 00:26:10,662
- Robin: YOU...
- Man #2: YOU.

645
00:26:10,662 --> 00:26:11,930
Robin: COME WITH ME.

646
00:26:11,930 --> 00:26:14,066
Man #2: UH-HUH.

647
00:26:14,066 --> 00:26:15,834
Robin: AND HELP ME...

648
00:26:15,834 --> 00:26:18,003
- Man #2: HELP YOU, YES.
- Robin: YES, FIND THESE.

649
00:26:18,003 --> 00:26:19,071
Man #2: (whistles)

650
00:26:19,071 --> 00:26:20,672
Robin: IT WAS HARD,

651
00:26:20,672 --> 00:26:23,208
BUT I RESORTED BACK
TO MY PAGEANTRY SKILLS

652
00:26:23,208 --> 00:26:25,811
AND REALIZED THAT EVEN IF
YOU DON'T KNOW FRENCH, SPANISH

653
00:26:25,811 --> 00:26:28,180
OR MAYBE EVEN ENGLISH,
A SMILE IS UNIVERSAL.

654
00:26:28,180 --> 00:26:29,781
AND I HAVE MONEY.

655
00:26:29,781 --> 00:26:31,383
I'M GONNA GIVE YOU SOME MONEY
AT THE END.

656
00:26:31,383 --> 00:26:32,617
- Man #2: MONEY?
- Robin: YEAH.

657
00:26:32,617 --> 00:26:33,719
- Man #2: ME?
- Robin: YEAH, YOU.

658
00:26:33,719 --> 00:26:35,387
Man #2: TRèS BON. OUI. YES.

659
00:26:35,387 --> 00:26:37,222
Robin: YEAH, YOU.
THAT'S HOW WE DO IT IN AMERICA.

660
00:26:37,222 --> 00:26:38,724
Man #2: YES, YES.

661
00:26:38,724 --> 00:26:41,026
♪♪♪

662
00:26:41,026 --> 00:26:42,794
Woman: UH, HOW LONG
HAVE YOU BEEN MODELING?

663
00:26:42,794 --> 00:26:44,229
Shannon: NOT VERY LONG.

664
00:26:44,229 --> 00:26:45,597
I WAS ONLY FOCUSED, LIKE,
ON HIGH SCHOOL--

665
00:26:45,597 --> 00:26:46,932
Woman: SHH.

666
00:26:46,932 --> 00:26:49,000
WHO'S LISTENING TO US? NOBODY.

667
00:26:49,000 --> 00:26:50,268
OKAY.

668
00:26:50,268 --> 00:26:51,770
SO IT'S SOMETHING
YOU LOVE, FASHION?

669
00:26:51,770 --> 00:26:52,938
Shannon: I LOVE IT,
I MEAN, EVEN IF...

670
00:26:52,938 --> 00:26:53,939
IF I COULD DRAW, I WOULD BE,
LIKE, A FASHION DESIGNER

671
00:26:53,939 --> 00:26:55,240
OR SOMETHING.

672
00:26:55,240 --> 00:26:57,209
- Woman: OKAY.
- Shannon: I LOVE IT.

673
00:26:57,209 --> 00:26:58,710
OKAY, MY LOVE,
THAT'S ENOUGH FOR ME TODAY.

674
00:26:58,710 --> 00:27:00,045
I WILL REMEMBER YOU,
IT'S A PLEASURE.

675
00:27:00,045 --> 00:27:01,880
Shannon: IT WAS SO NICE
MEETING YOU. THANK YOU.

676
00:27:01,880 --> 00:27:03,281
Kesse: GOIN'
STRAIGHT DOWN, THEN?

677
00:27:03,281 --> 00:27:05,150
Man: RIGHT THROUGH THERE.

678
00:27:05,150 --> 00:27:07,152
Kesse: AND THEN GO DOWN.

679
00:27:07,152 --> 00:27:08,920
Man: ELLE RECHERHCE LA MéTRO.

680
00:27:08,920 --> 00:27:09,988
Woman: OUI, OUI,
MAIS S'IL VOUS PLAîT,

681
00:27:09,988 --> 00:27:10,789
VISITEZ LE MAGASIN D'ABORD.

682
00:27:13,992 --> 00:27:15,293
Kesse: LOOK,
IT MAKES YOU YOUNG, HUH?

683
00:27:15,293 --> 00:27:16,328
Woman #2: YEAH.

684
00:27:16,328 --> 00:27:21,199
Adrianne: I DON'T CARE.

685
00:27:21,199 --> 00:27:23,935
I DON'T...

686
00:27:23,935 --> 00:27:26,204
AAH!

687
00:27:26,204 --> 00:27:28,240
Woman #2: YOU HAVE
THE LOTION HERE.

688
00:27:28,240 --> 00:27:30,208
Kesse: OOH.
AND WHAT DOES THIS DO?

689
00:27:30,208 --> 00:27:31,276
OKAY.

690
00:27:31,276 --> 00:27:33,612
I MISSED THE THIRD LOCATION

691
00:27:33,612 --> 00:27:35,013
BECAUSE I JUST LOST TRACK
OF TIME.

692
00:27:35,013 --> 00:27:37,182
I'M NOT WORRIED ABOUT
THE OTHER GIRLS.

693
00:27:37,182 --> 00:27:38,917
SO IF THEY FINISH EVERYTHING,
THEN THAT'S GOOD,

694
00:27:38,917 --> 00:27:40,085
BUT THAT DOESN'T MEAN
THAT THEY'RE

695
00:27:40,085 --> 00:27:41,086
AMERICA'S NEXT TOP MODEL.

696
00:27:41,086 --> 00:27:43,188
♪♪♪

697
00:27:43,188 --> 00:27:44,823
Elyse: BONJOUR.

698
00:27:44,823 --> 00:27:46,358
PHILLIPE ECOUVIER,
S'IL VOUS PLAîT.

699
00:27:46,358 --> 00:27:49,060
- Phillipe: BONJOUR.
- Elyse: BONJOUR.

700
00:27:49,060 --> 00:27:51,763
JE M'APPELLE ELYSE SEWELL.

701
00:27:51,763 --> 00:27:52,898
- Phillip: AH, OKAY.
- Kesse: HI. BONJOUR.

702
00:27:52,898 --> 00:27:53,899
JE M'APPELLE KESSE.

703
00:27:53,899 --> 00:27:55,901
Man: BUSY DAY?

704
00:27:55,901 --> 00:27:58,003
Kesse: OH, IT'S BEEN BUSY,
BUT IT'S BEEN A RUSH, YOU KNOW?

705
00:27:58,003 --> 00:27:59,271
Phillipe: CAN I SEE YOU WALKING?

706
00:28:07,112 --> 00:28:08,880
Elyse: CARRYING MYSELF
MORE CONFIDENTLY

707
00:28:08,880 --> 00:28:12,350
HAS BEEN A FORCED EFFORT,
AND I-I'VE DONE IT ON PURPOSE.

708
00:28:12,350 --> 00:28:14,052
AND I THINK IT MIGHT BE WORKING.

709
00:28:14,052 --> 00:28:17,255
♪♪♪

710
00:28:17,255 --> 00:28:18,657
Adrianne: I AM SO LOST.

711
00:28:22,160 --> 00:28:23,929
Woman: UH, I WOULD LIKE
TO TRY SOMETHING.

712
00:28:23,929 --> 00:28:25,197
Robin: OKAY.

713
00:28:27,799 --> 00:28:29,067
Woman: THANK YOU.

714
00:28:29,067 --> 00:28:31,269
Adrianne: ENGLISH,
S'IL VOUS PLAîT?

715
00:28:31,269 --> 00:28:33,371
NO?

716
00:28:33,371 --> 00:28:35,240
DOES ANYONE SPEAK ENGLISH?

717
00:28:37,642 --> 00:28:39,811
Adrianne: THIS MAN
WALKED UP TO ME IN THE STREET

718
00:28:39,811 --> 00:28:41,213
AND, LIKE, BRUSHED MY LEG
LIKE THERE WAS

719
00:28:41,213 --> 00:28:42,914
SOMETHING ON MY KNEE.

720
00:28:42,914 --> 00:28:44,216
I THOUGHT,
OH, THERE MIGHT HAVE BEEN

721
00:28:44,216 --> 00:28:45,350
SOMETHING ON MY KNEE.

722
00:28:45,350 --> 00:28:46,985
THEN HE PROCEEDED
TO TRY TO SHOVE HIS HAND

723
00:28:46,985 --> 00:28:48,887
UP MY SKIRT TOWARDS MY CROTCH.

724
00:28:48,887 --> 00:28:50,155
SO I WAS REALLY UPSET.

725
00:28:50,155 --> 00:28:52,290
I MEAN, I WAS RIGHT THERE
BY THE AGENCY, BUT I--

726
00:28:52,290 --> 00:28:54,025
I COULDN'T EVEN GO IN.

727
00:28:59,664 --> 00:29:03,394
♪♪♪

728
00:29:03,394 --> 00:29:05,230
Shannon: THE CHALLENGE WAS

729
00:29:05,230 --> 00:29:09,601
TO GO AND SEE ALL FIVE AGENCIES
IN THE TIME THAT WAS ALLOTTED.

730
00:29:09,601 --> 00:29:12,604
I MADE IT TO ALL THE AGENCIES
EVEN IF I WAS A FEW MINUTES LATE

731
00:29:12,604 --> 00:29:13,638
ON ONE OR NOT,
BUT I STILL MADE IT.

732
00:29:18,843 --> 00:29:21,579
Kesse: I'M HAVING A BLAST
IN PARIS, I AM.

733
00:29:21,579 --> 00:29:24,883
♪♪♪

734
00:29:24,883 --> 00:29:27,252
Adrianne: I WASN'T
AS FULLY CONFIDENT IN MYSELF.

735
00:29:27,252 --> 00:29:29,254
I JUST...

736
00:29:29,254 --> 00:29:30,655
I FEEL LIKE I CAN DO BETTER.

737
00:29:30,655 --> 00:29:34,392
OH, MERCI, MERCI, MERCI.

738
00:29:34,392 --> 00:29:35,426
Man: C'EST EXACT Là.

739
00:29:35,426 --> 00:29:36,494
C'EST EXACT Là.

740
00:29:36,494 --> 00:29:37,529
Adrianne: MERCI,
MERCI, MERCI.

741
00:29:37,529 --> 00:29:38,596
Man: C'EST BON.

742
00:29:38,596 --> 00:29:39,931
Adrianne: THANK YOU SO MUCH.

743
00:29:39,931 --> 00:29:41,900
I AM FROM CHICAGO, BUT--

744
00:29:41,900 --> 00:29:43,468
- Woman: CHICAGO?
- Adrianne: YES.

745
00:29:43,468 --> 00:29:46,471
YOU SAY IT LIKE ME. CHICAGO.

746
00:29:46,471 --> 00:29:47,372
Woman: (laughs)
WHAT'S THE EYE COLOR,

747
00:29:47,372 --> 00:29:48,873
BLUE-GRAY, SOMETHING?

748
00:29:48,873 --> 00:29:50,308
Adrianne: BLUE-GRAY.
THEY CHANGE.

749
00:29:50,308 --> 00:29:53,878
♪♪♪

750
00:29:53,878 --> 00:29:55,380
Elyse: OUR LAST GO SEE,

751
00:29:55,380 --> 00:29:57,916
UM, IT WAS AT A HOTEL,
AND I TOOK A LITTLE BIT OF TIME

752
00:29:57,916 --> 00:29:59,751
TO TIGHTEN UP MY LIP
AND PUT ON SOME MORE MAKEUP

753
00:29:59,751 --> 00:30:00,919
BEFORE I WENT IN.

754
00:30:00,919 --> 00:30:02,720
WHEN I WALKED INTO THE ROOM,
I HAD NO IDEA

755
00:30:02,720 --> 00:30:03,755
WHAT WAS GOING ON.

756
00:30:03,755 --> 00:30:04,989
Robin: OKAY.

757
00:30:04,989 --> 00:30:07,559
THIS IS THE LAST STOP.

758
00:30:07,559 --> 00:30:10,995
THIS IS A LITTLE APPRECIATION
FROM ME TO YOU FOR HELPING ME.

759
00:30:10,995 --> 00:30:13,631
- Man: MERCI.
- Robin: MERCI.

760
00:30:13,631 --> 00:30:15,934
- Man: MERCI.
- Robin: MERCI BEAUCOUP.

761
00:30:15,934 --> 00:30:18,736
SO... OH, THAT'S SWEET.

762
00:30:18,736 --> 00:30:20,838
Kesse: THANK YOU.

763
00:30:22,907 --> 00:30:26,811
Adrianne: I MISSED ONE TODAY.

764
00:30:29,013 --> 00:30:30,348
Shannon: ALL RIGHT, YOU GUYS,
WE HAVE A LETTER.

765
00:30:30,348 --> 00:30:31,382
Robin: OKAY.

766
00:30:31,382 --> 00:30:32,584
Shannon: WE HAVE A LETTER.

767
00:30:32,584 --> 00:30:34,852
UM, LET'S SEE.

768
00:30:34,852 --> 00:30:39,524
"WELCOME TO YOUR FINAL GO SEE,
A MEETING WITH THE JUDGES.

769
00:30:39,524 --> 00:30:41,960
PLEASE WAIT HERE
UNTIL FURTHER NOTICE."

770
00:30:48,566 --> 00:30:50,768
Kesse: I DON'T KNOW WHO COULD BE
ELIMINATED, SERIOUSLY.

771
00:30:50,768 --> 00:30:52,670
IT'S JUST... I DON'T KNOW.

772
00:30:52,670 --> 00:30:54,772
IT'S GONNA BE SHOCKING,
WHOEVER IT IS.

773
00:30:54,772 --> 00:30:57,342
YOU KNOW, FROM THIS POINT ON,
IT'S GONNA BE LIKE, DANG.

774
00:30:57,342 --> 00:31:01,946
Adrianne: YOU GUYS,
I DON'T WANT TO GO HOME.

775
00:31:01,946 --> 00:31:03,648
Robin: I DON'T GET NERVOUS
BECAUSE, UH,

776
00:31:03,648 --> 00:31:06,351
NERVOUSNESS IS NOT A...

777
00:31:06,351 --> 00:31:08,820
MY RELIGION TEACHES ME
THAT THAT'S NOT OF GOD.

778
00:31:08,820 --> 00:31:10,755
Adrianne: YOU BETTER
PRETEND THAT YOU MISS ME

779
00:31:10,755 --> 00:31:11,823
IF I LEAVE.

780
00:31:11,823 --> 00:31:13,591
Elyse: YOU BETTER
BE CAREFUL, GIRL.

781
00:31:13,591 --> 00:31:16,227
Adrianne: I'LL PRETEND
TO MISS YOU.

782
00:31:22,433 --> 00:31:24,736
Tyra: BONSOIR, LADIES.

783
00:31:25,269 --> 00:31:27,839
THIS WEEK YOU GUYS GOT A TASTE
OF THE JET-SET LIFE.

784
00:31:27,839 --> 00:31:30,441
YOU LEARNED HOW TO PUT
TOGETHER YOUR PORTFOLIO,

785
00:31:30,441 --> 00:31:33,344
YOU WENT ON GO SEES,
YOU DID A PHOTO SHOOT

786
00:31:33,344 --> 00:31:35,813
IN FRONT OF THE EIFFEL TOWER,
WHICH I THOUGHT WAS FIERCE

787
00:31:35,813 --> 00:31:37,515
'CAUSE I'VE NEVER
DONE THAT BEFORE.

788
00:31:37,515 --> 00:31:39,717
THE WINNER WILL RECEIVE
A REVLON CONTRACT,

789
00:31:39,717 --> 00:31:41,919
A CONTRACT
WITH WILHELMINA MODELS INC.

790
00:31:41,919 --> 00:31:44,689
AND A FASHION SPREAD
IN "MARIE CLAIRE" MAGAZINE.

791
00:31:44,689 --> 00:31:46,858
ONCE AGAIN,
WE HAVE OUR EXPERT JUDGES--

792
00:31:46,858 --> 00:31:47,992
JANICE DICKINSON.

793
00:31:47,992 --> 00:31:49,927
Janice: HEY.
BONJOUR, LADIES.

794
00:31:49,927 --> 00:31:52,630
Tyra: AND WE HAVE
BEAU QUILLIAN.

795
00:31:52,630 --> 00:31:53,498
BEAU QUILLIAN
IS THE FASHION EDITOR

796
00:31:53,498 --> 00:31:55,266
AT "MARIE CLAIRE."

797
00:31:55,266 --> 00:31:56,300
Beau: HI, LADIES.

798
00:31:56,300 --> 00:31:57,735
Tyra: WE HAVE
KIMORA LEE SIMMONS,

799
00:31:57,735 --> 00:32:00,605
WHO'S THE CREATIVE DIRECTOR
AND OWNER OF BABY PHAT FASHIONS,

800
00:32:00,605 --> 00:32:03,941
WHO ALSO TOOK PARIS BY STORM
AT THE TENDER AGE OF 13.

801
00:32:03,941 --> 00:32:08,279
AND, OF COURSE, EVERY WEEK
WE HAVE A SPECIAL GUEST JUDGE.

802
00:32:08,279 --> 00:32:09,580
THIS WEEK IT IS MARILYN.

803
00:32:09,580 --> 00:32:12,684
MARILYN HAS BEEN MY AGENT
AND KIMORA'S AGENT.

804
00:32:12,684 --> 00:32:15,887
WE'LL BRING YOU IN ONE BY ONE
FOR YOUR INDIVIDUAL EVALUATIONS.

805
00:32:15,887 --> 00:32:17,622
AFTER THAT,
THE JUDGES DELIBERATE,

806
00:32:17,622 --> 00:32:18,990
AND THEN WE'LL DECIDE
WHICH ONE OF YOU

807
00:32:18,990 --> 00:32:20,291
SHOULD BE ELIMINATED.

808
00:32:20,291 --> 00:32:21,993
ELYSE, YOU'RE FIRST.

809
00:32:22,527 --> 00:32:24,862
ELYSE, EARLIER TODAY
YOU COMPLETED YOUR TEST

810
00:32:24,862 --> 00:32:27,398
WHEN MARILYN SENT YOU
ALL AROUND PARIS ON GO SEES.

811
00:32:27,398 --> 00:32:29,300
Emma: HOW MANY OF THE GO SEES
DID YOU MANAGE TO DO TODAY?

812
00:32:29,300 --> 00:32:30,668
Elyse: I DID ALL OF THEM.

813
00:32:30,668 --> 00:32:32,503
Emma: OKAY, WELL DONE,
BECAUSE IT WAS HARD.

814
00:32:32,503 --> 00:32:35,239
OUR CLIENTS DESCRIBED YOU
AS NICE, OPEN, FRIENDLY.

815
00:32:35,239 --> 00:32:37,542
Tyra: WHOO-HOO, CHILD.

816
00:32:37,542 --> 00:32:38,843
YOU ALSO HAD
A SEXY LINGERIE PHOTO SHOOT

817
00:32:38,843 --> 00:32:40,011
WITH MICHEL HADDI.

818
00:32:40,011 --> 00:32:41,813
HERE'S WHAT WE THOUGHT
WAS THE BEST SHOT.

819
00:32:41,813 --> 00:32:42,947
WHAT DO YOU THINK?

820
00:32:42,947 --> 00:32:44,382
Elyse: OH, I JUST THINK
THE POSE IS AWKWARD.

821
00:32:44,382 --> 00:32:46,284
Janice: YOU HAVE TO STOP
PUTTING YOURSELF DOWN.

822
00:32:46,284 --> 00:32:47,318
WE'RE A PANEL OF JUDGES.

823
00:32:47,318 --> 00:32:48,953
WE'RE HERE TO JUDGE THE POSE.

824
00:32:48,953 --> 00:32:50,455
SO I'M GONNA SPANK YOU
FOR DOING THAT.

825
00:32:50,455 --> 00:32:51,956
I LOVE THE WAY YOU LOOK HERE.

826
00:32:51,956 --> 00:32:53,658
Tyra: I HAVE TO DISAGREE
WITH JANICE.

827
00:32:53,658 --> 00:32:54,959
I'M STILL LOOKING
AT MY PICTURES

828
00:32:54,959 --> 00:32:57,261
AND A LOT OF THE TIMES,
I'M, LIKE, I DON'T LIKE THAT.

829
00:32:57,261 --> 00:32:58,596
I COULDA DONE BETTER.

830
00:32:58,596 --> 00:32:59,964
SO I LIKE THE FACT
THAT YOU WERE HONEST.

831
00:32:59,964 --> 00:33:01,666
Marilyn: I LOVE IT
BECAUSE IT'S NOT POSED,

832
00:33:01,666 --> 00:33:03,935
AS WE FOUND OUT,
SO IT'S VERY MODERN.

833
00:33:03,935 --> 00:33:05,803
Tyra: UH, LET ME TELL YOU
WHAT THE PHOTOGRAPHER SAID.

834
00:33:05,803 --> 00:33:06,871
HE SAID THAT YOU WERE THE BEST.

835
00:33:06,871 --> 00:33:07,872
Janice: THERE YOU GO.

836
00:33:07,872 --> 00:33:09,307
Marilyn: BONJOUR.

837
00:33:09,307 --> 00:33:11,442
- Tyra: MERCI, ELYSE.
- Elyse: MERCI.

838
00:33:11,442 --> 00:33:12,910
Tyra: SHANNON, VENEZ ICI.

839
00:33:12,910 --> 00:33:14,579
Emma: SHE DID FOUR GO SEES.

840
00:33:14,579 --> 00:33:16,314
HOW MANY OF THOSE FOUR
DID YOU MAKE?

841
00:33:16,314 --> 00:33:16,981
Shannon: I MADE ALL FOUR.

842
00:33:16,981 --> 00:33:18,616
Emma: WELL DONE.

843
00:33:18,616 --> 00:33:22,353
OUR CLIENTS DESCRIBED YOU
AS BEAUTIFUL, BIG SMILE,

844
00:33:22,353 --> 00:33:23,554
BUT MAYBE TOO OBVIOUS.

845
00:33:23,554 --> 00:33:25,690
Tyra: TOO OBVIOUS
MEANS TOO PRETTY.

846
00:33:25,690 --> 00:33:28,559
IN AMERICA, IT'S FINE TO BE
SAFE AND PRETTY AND LA,

847
00:33:28,559 --> 00:33:30,561
BUT HERE YOU GOTTA...

848
00:33:30,561 --> 00:33:31,829
JUST FREAK IT UP A LITTLE BIT.

849
00:33:31,829 --> 00:33:33,264
Janice: GOTTA HAVE
THE EDGE, GIRL.

850
00:33:33,264 --> 00:33:34,932
Tyra: SO YOU DID
A SEXY LINGERIE SHOOT,

851
00:33:34,932 --> 00:33:36,567
AND HERE IS THE BEST SHOT.

852
00:33:36,567 --> 00:33:38,970
Janice: YOU WERE ALL OVER HIM
LIKE A CHEAP SUIT HERE.

853
00:33:38,970 --> 00:33:40,605
YOU GOT A THING FOR THIS BOY?

854
00:33:40,605 --> 00:33:42,273
Shannon: WELL, I DON'T KNOW.
I HAVE TO GET TO KNOW HIM, BUT--

855
00:33:42,273 --> 00:33:43,341
Tyra: I HEARD
HE'S A CHRISTIAN.

856
00:33:43,341 --> 00:33:44,275
Janice: CHRISTIANS WITH ABS.

857
00:33:44,275 --> 00:33:45,643
Tyra: (laughs)

858
00:33:45,643 --> 00:33:47,245
Shannon: I LIKE TO FEEL
HIS PECS, SO...

859
00:33:47,245 --> 00:33:49,947
Beau: IT STILL FEELS TO ME
LIKE YOU'RE, LIKE, INTO IT,

860
00:33:49,947 --> 00:33:51,716
BUT YOU'RE STILL
A LITTLE BIT AFRAID

861
00:33:51,716 --> 00:33:54,018
TO GO ALL THE WAY THERE.

862
00:33:54,018 --> 00:33:56,721
Emma: OKAY, ADRIANNE, TODAY YOU
WENT ON FOUR GO AND SEES.

863
00:33:56,721 --> 00:33:58,956
OUT OF THE FOUR GO SEES,
HOW MANY DID YOU MAKE?

864
00:33:58,956 --> 00:34:01,259
Adrianne: I MADE THREE.

865
00:34:01,259 --> 00:34:02,760
Emma: WHAT HAPPENED?

866
00:34:02,760 --> 00:34:05,429
Adrianne: UM, I'VE NEVER BEEN
ON A SUBWAY IN MY LIFE.

867
00:34:05,429 --> 00:34:07,899
AND THAT'S NO EXCUSE,
BUT IT WAS VERY HARD FOR ME.

868
00:34:07,899 --> 00:34:09,233
Emma: NONE OF THE OTHER GIRLS
HAVE BEEN ON THE MéTRO,

869
00:34:09,233 --> 00:34:10,234
AND SOME OF THEM MADE IT.

870
00:34:10,234 --> 00:34:12,670
Tyra: I DO NOT
UNDERSTAND THAT.

871
00:34:12,670 --> 00:34:15,306
I WAS ON TIME
LIKE MY LIFE DEPENDED ON IT.

872
00:34:15,306 --> 00:34:16,373
Janice: YOU'RE RIGHT, TYRA.

873
00:34:16,373 --> 00:34:17,909
THAT'S WHEN THE STRONG SURVIVE.

874
00:34:17,909 --> 00:34:19,710
AND THE STRONG MAKE IT.

875
00:34:19,710 --> 00:34:22,547
Emma: YOU WERE DESCRIBED
BY OUR CLIENTS AS STYLING BAD,

876
00:34:22,547 --> 00:34:25,449
WOULD LOOK BETTER IN JEANS.

877
00:34:25,449 --> 00:34:27,385
HOW DO YOU FEEL ABOUT THAT?

878
00:34:27,385 --> 00:34:28,619
Adrianne: LIKE, STYLING,
I AGREE.

879
00:34:28,619 --> 00:34:30,922
IT WAS PROBABLY BAD,
I'M A REALLY BIG TOMBOY.

880
00:34:30,922 --> 00:34:33,391
Tyra: IN PERSON TO ME,
I FEEL LIKE YOU'RE HIDING

881
00:34:33,391 --> 00:34:36,427
WHO YOU ARE, AND CLIENTS WANT TO
SEE MORE AND WHAT THEY CAN DO.

882
00:34:36,427 --> 00:34:38,396
DOES SHE HAVE GOOD SKIN?
IS SHE HIDING PIMPLES
BEHIND THAT FOREHEAD?

883
00:34:38,396 --> 00:34:39,730
